= Answer Key

=== Test 1 — Diagnostic

Identify whether each item is a complete sentence (✓) or a fragment (✗). Correct the fragments by adding a subject or a verb.

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 4fr, 1.5fr, 4fr),
  table.header[*\#*][*Original*][*S or F?*][*Correction*],
  [1], [My best friend always helps me with my homework.], [✓], [Complete sentence — no correction needed.],
  [2], [Is very kind and generous.], [✗], [Add subject: *She / He is very kind and generous.*],
  [3], [My friend and I always together at lunch.], [✗], [Add verb: *My friend and I are always together at lunch.*],
  [4], [We share the same hobbies and interests.], [✓], [Complete sentence — no correction needed.],
  [5], [Usually meet at the weekend to play football.], [✗], [Add subject: *We usually meet at the weekend to play football.*],
  [6], [Our friendship strong because we trust each other.], [✗], [Add verb: *Our friendship is strong because we trust each other.*],
)

=== Practice 4A — Fragment or Complete Sentence (textbook p15)

Identify each item as a complete sentence (✓) or a fragment (✗). Correct the fragments.

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 4fr, 1.5fr, 4fr),
  table.header[*\#*][*Original*][*S or F?*][*Correction*],
  [1], [Is very hot today even with the windows open.], [✗], [Add subject: *It is very hot today even with the windows open.*],
  [2], [Jose and Jin the smartest students in the class.], [✗], [Add verb: *Jose and Jin are the smartest students in the class.*],
  [3], [They study all the time.], [✓], [Complete sentence — no correction needed.],
  [4], [The baby finally sleepy.], [✗], [Add verb: *The baby is finally sleepy.*],
  [5], [She is closing her eyes.], [✓], [Complete sentence — no correction needed.],
  [6], [Ms. Woodbury, our grammar teacher, often late on Fridays.], [✗], [Add verb: *Ms. Woodbury, our grammar teacher, is often late on Fridays.*],
  [7], [Is important for students to get to class on time.], [✗], [Add subject: *It is important for students to get to class on time.*],
)

=== Practice 4B — Editing Practice (textbook p15)

Find and correct the five fragments in the paragraph *My Best Friend*.

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 4fr, 1fr, 5fr),
  table.header[*\#*][*Fragment*][*Issue*][*Correction*],
  [1], [Now live in different countries on different continents.], [Missing subject], [Add *We*: *We now live in different countries on different continents.*],
  [2], [Has three children.], [Missing subject], [Add *She*: *She has three children.*],
  [3], [Her son two years old,], [Missing verb], [Add *is*: *Her son is two years old,*],
  [4], [and her twin daughters three months old.], [Missing verb], [Add *are*: *and her twin daughters are three months old.*],
  [5], [Also telephone each other at least once a month.], [Missing subject], [Add *We*: *We also telephone each other at least once a month.*],
)

*Note:* A complete sentence must have at least one subject and one verb. If either is missing, the sentence is a fragment. The subject can sometimes follow the verb (e.g., *There is...*), but the key rule is: every sentence needs both a subject and a verb.
